Fillets: the meeting point of two stripes on their common face when one
contact line is periodic (mitcad#122).

ChFi3d_IntTraces intersects the contact lines of two stripes ending at the
same vertex on their common face, and among several intersections keeps,
for a periodic contact line (a fillet along a circle), the one whose
parameter is closest to the reference parameter, the end of that stripe's
surface data. That end may lie far beyond the vertex, on the extension of
the stripe (a torus extended by a quarter turn): two fillets meeting at a
shallow corner (an arc and a line at 10 degrees) then met at the far
intersection of the arc's contact circle with the line's contact line, and
the bevel between them (PerformTwoCornerbyInter) gave a self-intersecting
face. When the vertex is given (Check2dDistance) and the other, non-periodic
contact line prefers the other point, the point nearest to the vertex is
kept.
